Host expert path: prior work
----------------------------
src/ops/sparse_moe/host/ (host_nvfp4, host_moe_executor, host_moe_mailbox) derives
from the following works, each licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  * FreeToken authors (FlashML-org) -- https://github.com/FlashML-org/FreeToken
    (commit 555efd8) The NVFP4 W4A8 AVX-512 VNNI dot (dot_nvfp4_i8_avx512vnni,
    nvfp4_i8_grp4) and its int8 activation layout, adapted to the swizzled
    block-scale plane; the binary ready/done flag protocol of the GPU stream
    memory operations (done reset before each doorbell).

  * 1872183316 -- https://github.com/1872183316/ninfer-offload (commit 1fd5c39)
    The two-phase weight-major host MoE executor (HostMoeExecutor) and the
    mapped mailbox with cuStreamWriteValue32/cuStreamWaitValue32 inside the
    captured graph, here ported to NVFP4 W4A8 with a pinned pool.

src/ops/sparse_moe/host/host_nvfp4_avx2.cpp (the AVX2 forms of the NVFP4 dots)
follows the AVX2 NVFP4 row kernel of the following project, licensed under the
MIT License:

  * Niko1221 and the Strata contributors -- https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata
    Copyright (c) 2026 Niko1221 and the Strata contributors.
    src/kernels/cpu/nvfp4_avx2.cpp (commit f57c0ad): two nibble lookups per 16
    code bytes rebuilt into element order with 64-bit unpacks, the
    vpsignb + vpmaddubsw + vpmaddwd integer dot and the per-half broadcast of
    the sub-block scales (no gathers). This tree keeps the lane order and the
    operation order of its AVX-512 kernels so that both give identical bits.

