GGUF routed-expert formats and host kernels: prior work
-------------------------------------------------------
third_party/ggml-iq/ is ggml's reference code for the block formats of the GSQ-RCO
expert banks (block definitions, grids and sign tables, dequantizers, the Q8_0/Q8_K
reference quantizers and the generic dot products) from ggml commit
3cf03257f219afbe7334045ff7c6a06ac68c627d, as extracted by fngine (below):
  * The ggml authors -- https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
    Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors. MIT License (third_party/ggml-iq/LICENSE).

src/ops/sparse_moe/host/host_gguf.{h,cpp} and host_q8.{h,cpp} derive from:
  * satellitedown -- https://github.com/satellitedown/fngine (commit c20a885)
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; its CPU i-quant kernel files
    (src/cpu/iq_cpu.{h,cpp}, here host_gguf.{h,cpp}) are SPDX MIT as derivatives of
    ggml-cpu/arch/x86/quants.c. The AVX-512 VNNI/VBMI/BITALG decode-once kernels for
    IQ2_S, IQ3_XXS, IQ3_S, IQ4_XS, IQ4_NL and Q2_0 and the Q8_K/Q8_0 quantizers that
    are bit-identical to ggml's reference.

src/ops/moe_slots_gguf/ (the GPU Ops moe_slots_gguf and moe_grouped_gguf) derives from
the same fngine commit:
  * iq_device.cuh from src/kernels/moe/iq_device.cuh: device block structs, the
    dp4a sub-block decode (from ggml-cuda/vecdotq.cuh), the exact 8-element
    dequantization (from ggml-quants.c dequantize_row_*) and the q8_1-style activation
    quantizer (from ggml-cuda/quantize.cu); SPDX MIT for the ggml portions, ggml commit
    3cf03257f219afbe7334045ff7c6a06ac68c627d (The ggml authors, MIT License);
  * decode_kernels.cu from src/kernels/moe/moe_decode.cu (hot-expert gate/up and down
    GEMV kernels) and grouped_kernels.cu from src/kernels/moe/moe_grouped_gemm.cu and
    src/kernels/moe/moe_prefill.cu (BF16-dequant mma grouped GEMMs, per-expert grouping);
    Apache License, Version 2.0. The routing/work-list, merge and launch code is
    rewritten for this tree's Op interface; each file lists its changes.

The gguf_* numeric format names and ids and the gguf_blocks_v1 layout
(tools/artifact/formats.py, layouts.py) follow:
  * iamwavecut -- https://github.com/iamwavecut/ninfer-all (commit 5ed86df)
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The 3-bit GSQ path of Qwen3.8-27B (q3_g128_fp16: tools/convert/qwen3_8_27b/, the
official recipe qwen3_8_27b_gsq3 and src/ops/linear/q3/) follows the work of:
  * roofkid -- https://github.com/roofkid/ninfer-4080
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The Q3G128_F16S code layout (signed
    codes, 48 bytes per 128-code group, FP16 group scale) and the design of the small-T
    tensor-core and staged GEMV routes; this tree's kernels keep the codes exact and
    apply the multiplier in FP32 (see the comments in q3_linear.cu).
  * The weights are ISTA-DASLab's Qwen3.8-27B-3Bit-GSQ
    (https://huggingface.co/ISTA-DASLab/Qwen3.8-27B-3Bit-GSQ), imported verbatim.

